  "notes": "USAGE:\nPrimarily used in legal and social welfare contexts. The word carries a strong nuance of moral reform and returning to society as a productive member.\n\nFORMS:\n{更|こう} (renew, change) + {生|せい} (life). Literally \"renewing one's life.\"\n\nWATCH OUT:\nSeveral words share the reading こうせい — {公正|こうせい} (fairness), {構成|こうせい} (composition), {恒星|こうせい} (fixed star). The kanji {更生|こうせい} specifically refers to rehabilitation.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {更生|こうせい}{施設|しせつ}: rehabilitation facility\n- {更生|こうせい}{保護|ほご}: rehabilitation and protection\n- {社会|しゃかい}{復帰|ふっき}と{更生|こうせい}: social reintegration and rehabilitation\n- {更生|こうせい}の{道|みち}: the path to reform",
